  "narration": "Start with the actual world: where the firm is today. Around it sits a ring of feasible worlds, the ways the next few years could plausibly go. Further out are remote worlds. Possible, but not worth planning around. A tactic is a move that wins in one of those worlds. A strategy holds up across most of them. And a no-regrets move is good in every feasible world. Box, in the language of modal logic: true wherever we could end up.",
